1249
00:58:16.210 --> 00:58:18.770
I have an observation about this scene.

1250
00:58:19.150 --> 00:58:23.070
Jim keeps saying spin serve, spin serve.

1251
00:58:23.650 --> 00:58:24.830
That is not a thing.

1252
00:58:25.110 --> 00:58:26.170
I looked it up.

1253
00:58:26.990 --> 00:58:30.290
Spin is not reserved for a serve.

1254
00:58:30.290 --> 00:58:37.410
And of the top five table tennis serves, only three of the five involve any spin.

1255
00:58:37.630 --> 00:58:38.910
And I'll tell you what they are.

1256
00:58:39.030 --> 00:58:42.170
Number one, the short side spin pendulum serve.

1257
00:58:42.650 --> 00:58:46.730
Number two, the short side spin reverse pendulum serve.

1258
00:58:48.070 --> 00:58:51.850
Number three is the fast, no spin cross serve.

1259
00:58:52.270 --> 00:58:56.330
Number four is the fast, no spin down the line serve.

1260
00:58:56.970 --> 00:59:00.210
And number five is the long side spin serve.

1261
00:59:00.570 --> 00:59:03.970
So there's no such thing as just spin serve.

1262
00:59:04.190 --> 00:59:06.970
You have to be more specific, Jim.

1263
00:59:07.210 --> 00:59:08.910
Is it a short side spin?

1264
00:59:08.910 --> 00:59:09.950
Is it a pendulum?

1265
00:59:10.350 --> 00:59:11.990
Is it a long side spin?

1266
00:59:12.370 --> 00:59:16.290
And by the way, just because you're putting spin on it doesn't mean you're

1267
00:59:16.290 --> 00:59:20.650
mastering the game because there's a couple of great serves that involve no spin at all.

1268
00:59:20.850 --> 00:59:26.250
I don't know why I felt the need to put Jim in his place about this spin serve,

1269
00:59:26.410 --> 00:59:29.470
but he was just saying it with such authority.

1270
00:59:30.630 --> 00:59:32.170
And it's not a thing, Jim.

1271
00:59:32.310 --> 00:59:32.770
It's not a thing.

1272
00:59:33.430 --> 00:59:36.890
Well, don't tell my husband that because he thinks the spin serve is where it's at.

1273
00:59:37.170 --> 00:59:39.370
He's going to spin it on over.

1274
00:59:40.510 --> 00:59:44.210
Listen, it's just that there needs to be more specificity.

1275
00:59:44.210 --> 00:59:48.330
Well, I'm going to tell him that next time he's playing while I'm trying to eat at the

1276
00:59:48.330 --> 00:59:49.050
ping pong table.

1277
00:59:49.370 --> 00:59:49.730
Please do.

1278
00:59:49.850 --> 00:59:51.070
You put him in his place.

1279
00:59:51.390 --> 00:59:53.130
Josh, that's not the long spin.

1280
00:59:53.850 --> 00:59:54.630
Side spin.

1281
00:59:55.070 --> 00:59:55.850
Short spin.

1282
00:59:56.010 --> 00:59:57.010
That's a short spin.

1283
00:59:57.390 --> 00:59:58.130
There you go.

1284
00:59:58.690 --> 01:00:00.110
Well, Jim says he's ready.

1285
01:00:00.530 --> 01:00:02.070
I'm going to go play Daryl.

1286
01:00:02.190 --> 01:00:04.130
Pam's so excited they go down to the warehouse.

1287
01:00:04.130 --> 01:00:07.050
And right away, it's not going Jim's way.

1288
01:00:07.270 --> 01:00:10.950
And Kelly starts doing all of her smack talk, trash talk.

1289
01:00:11.130 --> 01:00:12.210
She's making up a song.

1290
01:00:12.290 --> 01:00:13.450
Hey, hey, you, you.

1291
01:00:13.550 --> 01:00:14.710
I don't like your boyfriend.

1292
01:00:15.050 --> 01:00:16.250
She's doing a whole thing.

1293
01:00:16.810 --> 01:00:17.630
Pam has had it.

1294
01:00:18.070 --> 01:00:18.270
Yeah.

1295
01:00:18.630 --> 01:00:22.790
She's like, you and me right now, we're going to play.

1296
01:00:23.350 --> 01:00:24.770
And they are both horrible.

1297
01:00:25.310 --> 01:00:26.570
We had a fan question.

1298
01:00:34.010 --> 01:00:35.570
Let me say this.

1299
01:00:35.910 --> 01:00:40.170
Mindy and I were not great at ping pong, but we weren't that bad at ping pong.

1300
01:00:40.290 --> 01:00:43.830
So we were pretending to be that bad.

1301
01:00:43.970 --> 01:00:48.310
And the point was that we would never get past a certain number of volleys.

1302
01:00:48.430 --> 01:00:50.090
Are they called volleys in ping pong?

1303
01:00:50.450 --> 01:00:51.630
You should know.

1304
01:00:53.210 --> 01:00:55.970
Oh, I didn't get that far in my research.

1305
01:00:57.710 --> 01:01:03.690
And also, I know that John was actually good at ping pong, and he had to pretend to be not as good as he was.

1306
01:01:04.110 --> 01:01:04.350
Yes.

1307
01:01:04.630 --> 01:01:11.390
And by the way, we played a lot of ping pong while we were just waiting for various camera setups and things like that.

1308
01:01:11.550 --> 01:01:18.870
This was a really fun day of shooting, actually, because we had this toy, which then stayed in the warehouse and we would play.

1309
01:01:19.250 --> 01:01:24.810
Well, and there are a lot of deleted scenes of all the other office members playing ping pong that didn't make it in.

1310
01:01:24.810 --> 01:01:29.190
And Phyllis and Stanley play at the makeshift ping pong table up in the conference room.

1311
01:01:29.370 --> 01:01:30.670
Meredith has a turn.

1312
01:01:30.970 --> 01:01:33.390
I yell off camera, I'm next!

1313
01:01:33.590 --> 01:01:36.890
So it's like everyone is getting in there to play ping pong.

1314
01:01:37.350 --> 01:01:40.290
Lady, the deposition is almost over.

1315
01:01:40.290 --> 01:01:52.390
And it's so sad because they've read David Wallace's testimony about whether or not he was ever really going to hire Michael for this corporate position.

1316
01:01:52.570 --> 01:01:57.510
And you can tell in the testimony that David is really struggling to admit this.

1317
01:01:57.650 --> 01:02:00.950
But the truth is, Michael was never a real contender.

1318
01:02:00.950 --> 01:02:04.630
Yeah, David says, listen, come on, he's a nice guy.

1319
01:02:05.010 --> 01:02:05.550
Yeah.

1320
01:02:06.030 --> 01:02:11.890
And he didn't want to have to go on record saying truthfully, Michael isn't anyone he considered.

1321
01:02:12.170 --> 01:02:21.070
But you know what's interesting is of all of that crushing information, what Michael heard was that David Wallace called him a nice guy.

1322
01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:21.830
Yeah.

1323
01:02:22.130 --> 01:02:31.250
And when Jan's lawyer says, wouldn't you agree with Ms. Levinson that the company exhibits a pattern of disrespect towards its employees?

1324
01:02:31.610 --> 01:02:34.850
Michael says, absolutely not.

1325
01:02:35.210 --> 01:02:35.790
Yeah.

1326
01:02:36.010 --> 01:02:38.150
He tanks her lawsuit.

1327
01:02:38.530 --> 01:02:40.170
There goes the $4 million.

1328
01:02:41.170 --> 01:02:44.430
Now they're only going to be able to get Chinese food for dinner.

1329
01:02:44.430 --> 01:02:47.130
Oh, it's going to be a rough car ride home.

1330
01:02:47.330 --> 01:02:54.750
But there is a very sweet scene where David Wallace goes up to Michael and is like, hey, I'm really sorry that you got drug into this.

1331
01:02:54.870 --> 01:02:55.930
I never wanted that.

1332
01:02:56.390 --> 01:02:57.670
And Michael's like, it's OK.

1333
01:02:58.170 --> 01:03:02.850
There is this moment, though, Jenna, where David is like the father Michael never had.

1334
01:03:03.210 --> 01:03:05.630
And it looks like Michael is trying not to cry.

1335
01:03:05.830 --> 01:03:05.990
Yeah.

1336
01:03:06.150 --> 01:03:08.930
Like when your dad comes up to you and says, I'm sorry, buddy.

1337
01:03:09.170 --> 01:03:09.570
You OK?

1338
01:03:09.830 --> 01:03:10.710
It's like that moment.

1339
01:03:11.210 --> 01:03:11.370
Yeah.

1340
01:03:11.370 --> 01:03:15.570
And Michael's like, for the record, I think you're a nice guy, too.

1341
01:03:15.970 --> 01:03:17.850
It's a really sweet scene.

1342
01:03:18.270 --> 01:03:18.870
It is.

1343
01:03:19.210 --> 01:03:24.510
I have a great little behind the scenes trivia for you for that car ride home with Michael and Jan.

1344
01:03:24.890 --> 01:03:25.770
Ooh, tell me.

1345
01:03:26.230 --> 01:03:31.230
Lester said that they had put lipstick cameras in the PT Cruiser for that car ride home.

1346
01:03:31.470 --> 01:03:31.890
Mm-hmm.

1347
01:03:32.230 --> 01:03:36.250
And when they got the footage back, it was all just completely dark.

1348
01:03:36.250 --> 01:03:41.370
The little light that they had put in the car, like on the dashboard where you couldn't see it,

1349
01:03:41.530 --> 01:03:44.410
it was going to illuminate Melora and Steve's faces.

1350
01:03:44.650 --> 01:03:46.990
I guess there was something wrong with the light.

1351
01:03:47.130 --> 01:03:48.410
And it clicked off.

1352
01:03:48.550 --> 01:03:50.130
And all the footage was dark.

1353
01:03:50.270 --> 01:03:50.770
Oh, no.

1354
01:03:50.890 --> 01:03:58.050
So the only footage they had of that car ride scene was from the follow car that was in front of them.

1355
01:03:58.230 --> 01:03:58.510
Right?

1356
01:03:58.850 --> 01:03:59.250
Yes.

1357
01:03:59.250 --> 01:04:04.870
So they had a car in front of them filming them, and that's the only camera that worked.

1358
01:04:05.210 --> 01:04:07.610
And I actually really like it.

1359
01:04:07.710 --> 01:04:12.770
And they talked about this a little bit in the commentary that it made it seem just way more real.

1360
01:04:13.030 --> 01:04:13.710
Mm-hmm.

1361
01:04:14.070 --> 01:04:18.150
That there was this distance between the camera and what was happening.

1362
01:04:18.310 --> 01:04:21.050
Kind of like what Randall talked about when he was on.

1363
01:04:21.250 --> 01:04:25.170
The further away you were, the more intimate the moment feels to the viewer.

1364
01:04:25.630 --> 01:04:26.110
Absolutely.

1365
01:04:26.110 --> 01:04:34.810
This episode ends with an epic ping pong match between Dwight and Mose, who has left Shroop Farms,

1366
01:04:34.890 --> 01:04:36.230
I believe, for the first time.

1367
01:04:36.230 --> 01:04:38.210
We're seeing him off the farm.

1368
01:04:39.590 --> 01:04:42.690
They are playing ping pong in the warehouse.

1369
01:04:43.110 --> 01:04:44.830
It's clearly after hours.

1370
01:04:44.830 --> 01:04:45.570
It's dark.

1371
01:04:45.710 --> 01:04:46.790
Not all the lights are on.

1372
01:04:46.910 --> 01:04:49.210
And they are amazing.

1373
01:04:49.710 --> 01:04:55.130
We had a fan question, Angela, from Ben S., Keith N., Bethany M., and Kai B.

1374
01:04:56.010 --> 01:05:00.090
Were Rain and Mike Schur actually playing ping pong in this scene?

1375
01:05:00.310 --> 01:05:01.470
Are they that good?

1376
01:05:02.170 --> 01:05:02.770
No.

1377
01:05:03.330 --> 01:05:03.730
No.

1378
01:05:04.050 --> 01:05:05.510
This was all CGI.

1379
01:05:05.510 --> 01:05:11.090
I think by this time, they had learned how hard it was to actually film actors playing ping pong.

1380
01:05:11.230 --> 01:05:12.730
So that was CGI.

1381
01:05:13.450 --> 01:05:13.710
Yeah.

1382
01:05:13.950 --> 01:05:19.770
Those guys were just moving their arms, and they put the ball in digitally in poSt.

1383
01:05:19.770 --> 01:05:24.250
Before we wrap up this episode, you guys, there is a deleted scene that is delicious.

1384
01:05:24.810 --> 01:05:30.810
It's Creed's turn to practice ping pong with Jim in the conference room at Dunder Mifflin.

1385
01:05:31.350 --> 01:05:33.050
And Creed's like, yeah, I played.

1386
01:05:33.170 --> 01:05:34.290
I learned to play in Cambodia.

1387
01:05:34.910 --> 01:05:35.650
Jim's like, great.

1388
01:05:35.870 --> 01:05:36.550
They start playing.

1389
01:05:36.730 --> 01:05:38.670
Creed loses a point right out of the gate.

1390
01:05:38.970 --> 01:05:40.210
Starts taking off his shirt.

1391
01:05:40.470 --> 01:05:41.410
Jim's like, hold up.

1392
01:05:41.590 --> 01:05:43.070
What's happening?

1393
01:05:43.070 --> 01:05:45.890
And Creed's like, but this isn't strip pong?

1394
01:05:46.310 --> 01:05:48.750
And Jim's like, no, no, no.

1395
01:05:49.770 --> 01:05:50.750
Creed's like, okay.

1396
01:05:51.090 --> 01:05:51.570
Wow.

1397
01:05:52.250 --> 01:05:56.030
Creed thought when you play ping pong, you have to strip when you lose a point.

1398
01:05:56.230 --> 01:05:56.930
Oh, that's funny.

1399
01:05:57.010 --> 01:05:58.090
I wish that stayed in.

1400
01:05:58.290 --> 01:05:58.870
I know.

1401
01:05:59.130 --> 01:06:00.150
That's what she said.

1402
